invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: check_required stops comparing the groups a KeyShareEntry named
  against supported_groups, so a share for this build's group parses
  when the client never listed the group. RFC 9846 §4.2.8 forbids the
  client to send one and names illegal_parameter for a server that
  checks, and the settled rule is that this server checks.
  test/srv_parser_tests.h lists secp256r1 alone beside an x25519 share
  and requires the alert.

--- old
    if ((ch->shares & (uint8_t)~ch->groups) != 0) {
        return srv_refuse(alert, ALERT_ILLEGAL_PARAMETER);
    }
--- new
    // A share for a group supported_groups did not list is srv_select's
    // to notice.
